      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CHATEAU DANCER (5) ran below expectations last time at Sandown-Hillside, finishing sixth and beaten 6 lengths starting at $7, but the fact she started that price in town is an indication of the class edge she has on rivals here. Fitter for the two runs back and stepping up to this trip looks perfect. CLYDEBANK ROBBER (1) has had way too many chances - 57 starts - but is going as well as he's ever gone and there's no reason he won't look a hope at some point once again. LUCKY CHANCE (2) was in a different class last time with a dominant all-the-way win by 2.5 lengths at Coleraine over 3600m. Must be included. TRULY FIERCE (9) never looked likely on debut but will be better for that and she looks to have a little more upside than several rivals here.",
